<p>LONDON UNDER SIEGE</p>
</div>
<div class="unmargined" style="font-family: 'Anton'; font-size: 380%; margin: 2px 0 5px;">
<p>Armed Forces deployed against avian mutants</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span>
<div class="page">
<p>Bumaro finally came out after ten days. He exited the spire just after dawn, peeked at one of the craters, and then immediately retreated back inside. Whatever the Cogworks have been doing in the crater, it's nearing its conclusion. There's fewer and fewer of them every day and I've noticed holes in the guard shifts.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br />
I've assembled a plan to kidnap Bumaro. For whatever reason, the Cogworks still use the latrine &#8212; and do so in packs. I've made a few pipe bombs from the supplies I took off Wondertainment's corpse and investigated the sewer system; it stinks like shit and murders my knees, but offers direct access to a public toilet near the craters. I'll make my way there by nightfall. As the guard shift changes, I'll plant the pipe bombs in the latrine, then use the cover of darkness to get near Bumaro's chambers. If my IEDs work, they'll melt the brass right off Bumaro's men, and I can use what little remains in Wondertainment's squirt gun to incapacitate him and get him into the sewers.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br />
It feels good to be doing this again. I remember when Fritz taught me how to make pipe bombs, damn near sixty years ago. Almost blew my hands and his head off with a short fuse.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br />
To do: Stay frosty.</p>
</div>
